  "worked_solution": "First, multiplying each component of $r$ by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}r & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{3}r)\\cdot s & =5\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-7)+2\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5-21+12-2 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
